  "description": "K-05 v1.16, a minor version of the data-access calls (T-1391: K-09 v1.10's open gap 147, from T-1373's round 2 and the action-layer engineer's round 1 FAIL; DL-751, DL-752, DL-754). It only adds to v1.15 (data-access.v1.15.schema.json, frozen and unchanged, referred to here, which refers on to every earlier version down to v1): every v1.15 definition is here under its own name, by reference, save the two restated: readOutboxRowWritten.response, which takes two optional fields, and readOutboxRowWritten.exchange, to refer to it and to the new readOutboxRowWritten.v1dot16Response. So every v1 to v1.15 exchange is a v1.16 exchange. Added: readOutboxRowWritten's answer names the written row's recipient and send class (README item 70), as K-04 v1's outbox_rows.recipient_handle_id and send_class store them, so a repeated safety record names the first record's rows with their recipients (K-09 v1.10 default 175): recipientHandleId, a K-08 v1 handleRef, never a number or an address, and sendClass, both null exactly when written is false. A v1.16 call always writes both (readOutboxRowWritten.v1dot16Response). The call keeps v1.4's role and scope (README item 41) and still reads no words: of the row, its id, recipient_handle_id and send_class alone. No call, state, column, grant, index or migration is added. Not model-facing, so number and length limits are schema rules here. Owner: the architect.",
